KWin: apply an interactive move at most twice per frame (6.7.5 port of patches/kwin/0060 v2, 2026-10-17)

The first pointer position after a frame started is applied at once, as before; later ones until
the next frame starts are held back and only the latest is applied when that frame starts
(Compositor::aboutToPrepareFrame), when the move ends, or before a key acts on it. A 4000 Hz mouse
moved the window 4000 times a second, and every move went to the window management clients:
plasmashell's task models froze for seconds behind them. KWIN_MOVE_COALESCE=0: as before.
Measured on 6.7.91 (v1, which held every position): guest KWin -33 %, plasmashell -80 % CPU per
4000 Hz drag, positions unchanged (findings/kwin-move-per-event-2026-10-17.md).

